{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>There is no remembrance.</b> If you say: had this new thing been so in ancient days, as we heard — they heard. \"There is no remembrance of the former ones; nor indeed of the later ones, with the last of the later ones, until here.\" These are Solomon's words in summary, and now he begins to clarify all the matters that come to mind."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:52.486179486Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}